WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.120
Hank: Good morning, John

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:03.759
First, I don't have time to analyze the whole
census right now.

00:00:03.759 --> 00:00:04.759
I really wish I did.

00:00:04.759 --> 00:00:05.759
And I'm going to.

00:00:05.759 --> 00:00:07.669
But right now I don't have time 'cause there's
a lot to do today.

00:00:07.669 --> 00:00:14.719
But I will say: That until your unnecessarily
negative campaign started, my hair was winning

00:00:14.719 --> 00:00:19.170
handily and now, surprise, surprise, it's
losing.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.180
Obviously this isn't a thing that matters.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.180
It's not a big deal.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:25.760
But I will say that if my hair ends up losing
it is an indictment to the entire process

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:26.790
of democracy.

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:28.680
If you look at the daily trends, and yes!

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:29.900
You can look at daily trends!

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.960
I love this survey, I'm so excited to analyze
it!

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.649
My hair was kicking your hair's butt, everyday,
until you made your video.

00:00:35.649 --> 00:00:37.480
Second, book towers.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:38.480
Oh.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.100
My God.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.789
We got so many amazing, astounding book towers.

00:00:43.789 --> 00:00:49.329
Like, there was almost 900 book towers sent
to hankandjohn@gmail.com.

00:00:49.329 --> 00:00:51.079
And they are all beautiful.

00:00:51.079 --> 00:00:55.260
Some of them make me uncomfortable with how
amazing they are.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:58.909
To all the people who were able to make Book
Towers: Thank you for putting your time and

00:00:58.909 --> 00:00:59.909
effort into it.

00:00:59.909 --> 00:01:03.079
I'm very sad that there can only be ten winners.

00:01:03.079 --> 00:01:05.610
But that's the rule I made up.

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:08.120
So, where would we be without rules?

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:11.380
I will say though, that many of the winners
appeared to be violating one of the rules,

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.680
which is: Don't do anything that might be
dangerous.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:18.410
And I can't imagine you built these towers
without standing on one of the steps of the

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:20.460
ladder that says "This is not a step".

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:22.850
But I don't have any way of knowing that for
sure, so I'm giving you the benefit of the

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.990
doubt that you didn't do anything dangerous.

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:25.990
Fingers crossed.

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:27.570
[phone noise] Who texted me?

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:30.630
Without further ado, though here are the winners
for the tallest towers.

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:34.790
We have Abby at #1 with a 483 centimeter tall
tower.

00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:38.030
She says that no part of the tower is touching
the wall and I'm trusting her.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:40.540
This one from Abby, Emma, Drew, Sue and Rob.

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:41.540
This one from Scott.

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:42.540
This one from Pete.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:43.600
This one from Josh.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:47.590
And we're gonna add in Steve just because
Josh and Steve's were very close together.

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:51.600
Choosing most styling was ridiculous difficult
because, of course, it's subjective and there

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.140
were a lot of amazing submissions.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:55.140
But here's what we're going with:

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:58.870
We've got Heather and Michelle's Nerdfighter
sign and DFTBA.

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:00.740
Lauren's Christmas tree of books.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:05.700
"The Arched Tower of Twists", from Morton,
"The Rocket", from Alexa Vlada.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:09.590
And Abby and Katie's amazing recreation of
Minas Tirith.

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:14.310
Which, remarkably, was not the only recreation
of Minas Tirith that was submitted.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:16.560
I had to have two honorable mentions, though.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:21.519
One, for engineering which goes to Brian because
this book tower doesn't look like it should

00:02:21.519 --> 00:02:22.519
work.

00:02:22.519 --> 00:02:25.540
That's just really remarkable to have a three
legged book tower this tall.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:30.069
And the other goes to the Nerdcrafteria Minecraft
server which had over 30 people working for

00:02:30.069 --> 00:02:35.400
days to build this really remarkable Minecraft
book tower.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.800
That I have very much enjoyed exploring and
it's full of surprises.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:39.800
If you wanna go check.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:40.800
it.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.830
out., so you can go to mc.nerdcrafteria.com

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:43.830
Third thing.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.900
NerdCon: Stories is coming up, and I recently
was talking about it and I said Cassandra

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:47.900
Clare was gonna be there.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:48.900
She's not.

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:50.010
I was wrong.

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:51.010
I apologize.

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:53.239
But there are gonna be many other amazing
people there.

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:55.420
We've got Holly Black, Mara Wilson, M.T.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:03:00.219
Anderson, the Welcome to Night Vale folks,
Nalo Hopkinson, Jacqueline Woodson, Rainbow

00:03:00.219 --> 00:03:04.900
Rowell, John Scalzi, Stephanie Perkins, Pat
Rothfuss and me and John.

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:05.900
And more and more and more.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:07.599
It's gonna be great.

00:03:07.599 --> 00:03:08.889
Fourth.

00:03:08.889 --> 00:03:10.120
Let's go get on an airplane!

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.120
Okay, bye.

